---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Pool from "../components/Pool.astro";
import Coverage from "../components/Coverage.astro";
// README.md, "Getting started" and "Run the judge locally". No release commit exists yet, so the SHA stays a placeholder.
const commands = {
 judge: `# .github/workflows/ludion-judge.yml
name: ludion-judge
on:
  pull_request:
    paths: [package-lock.json]
permissions:
  contents: read
# A newer push cancels the judgement of an older head.
concurrency:
  group: ludion-judge-\${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}
  cancel-in-progress: true
jobs:
  judge:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 15
    steps:
      - uses: Ludion-ai/ludion@<release commit SHA>
        with:
          mode: judge`,
 comment: `# .github/workflows/ludion-judge-comment.yml
name: ludion-judge-comment
on:
  workflow_run:
    workflows: [ludion-judge]
    types: [completed]
permissions:
  actions: read
  contents: read
  pull-requests: write
# One comment run at a time per PR branch, so two runs cannot both post a comment.
concurrency:
  group: ludion-judge-comment-\${{ github.event.workflow_run.head_repository.full_name }}-\${{ github.event.workflow_run.head_branch }}
  cancel-in-progress: false
jobs:
  comment:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 5
    steps:
      - uses: Ludion-ai/ludion@<the same release commit SHA>
        with:
          mode: comment`,
 source: "git clone https://github.com/Ludion-ai/ludion.git\ncd ludion\nnpm ci\nnpm run build -w ludion-ai",
 local: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js judge --before /path/to/app-main --after /path/to/app-pr --files package.json,package-lock.json",
};
---
<Base title="Judge your npm dependency PRs | Ludion" description="Add the Ludion judge to a repository as two GitHub workflows, or run it locally against two checkouts. A preview that only comments; not released yet.">
 <article class="start-page wrap">
  <header class="page-intro"><h1>Judge your npm dependency PRs.</h1><p class="intro">Add two workflows to a repository, or run the judge locally against two checkouts. Preview: comments only; nothing is merged.</p></header>
  <Pool>
   <section class="sync" aria-labelledby="workflows">
    <div class="install"><h2 id="workflows">Add two workflows</h2><p class="where">Not released yet · No release commit exists yet. The action needs one, because only a release commit carries the bundled judge; at any other commit it stops with an error. When one is published, pin its full 40-character SHA, not a tag or branch, in both workflows.</p><p>The first judges with read access only and runs nothing from the PR:</p><div class="command primary-command"><pre class="yaml" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="The judging workflow"><code id="judge-workflow">{commands.judge}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="judge-workflow" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy the judging workflow" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p class="wiring">The second posts the result. It runs from your default branch after each judge run, checks the result as untrusted data, and keeps one comment per PR up to date:</p><div class="command primary-command"><pre class="yaml" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="The comment workflow"><code id="comment-workflow">{commands.comment}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="comment-workflow" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy the comment workflow" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p class="wiring">A change to that SHA (from Dependabot, for example) is an update to Ludion itself: review it like any dependency update, and do not auto-merge it. The judge is not a required check unless you make it one.</p></div>
    <aside class="path" aria-labelledby="judge-path"><h3 id="judge-path" class="visually-hidden">What the judge does</h3><ol class="flow"><li><span class="step-title">Read</span><span class="step-detail">The PR's package.json and package-lock.json, before and after</span></li><li><span class="step-title">Check</span><span class="step-detail">Provenance, publisher, install scripts, MAL- records, deprecation, new dependencies</span></li><li><span class="step-title">Comment</span><span class="step-detail">One verdict, with when the wait ends and what was not checked</span></li></ol></aside>
   </section>
   <p class="coverage">npm only · Parts of gates 1, 2 and 4, and the wait. Gate 3, building and testing, is not run, so the judge never says an update can be applied.</p>
   <section class="reference" aria-labelledby="setup-details"><h2 id="setup-details">Running it, and its limits</h2>
    <details open><summary><span>Run the judge locally</span><span class="summary-note">Two checkouts, before and after</span></summary><div class="detail-body"><p>The published npm ludion-ai 0.1.4 release is the earlier lesson product, which ended on 2026-10-28; no release of the judge is on npm yet. Build this repository (Node 24):</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="source-command">{commands.source}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="source-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy build commands" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>Then give the judge two checkouts of your project, before and after the update, and the files the update changes:</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="judge-command">{commands.local}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="judge-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy judge command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>Exit codes: 0 ready except build (gates 1, 2 and 4 found nothing and the wait is over); 3 wait; 1 stop or undecidable, also when a lookup fails or --files is missing; 2 the inputs could not be read. --json gives the whole judgement. A pnpm-lock.yaml is read as the set of versions it adds, which is always undecidable.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><span>Limits</span><span class="summary-note">What the action reads</span></summary><div class="detail-body"><p>GitHub-hosted Linux runners: the action needs gh, jq, unzip, GNU date and Node 22 or later. Only the root package.json and package-lock.json, and each changed */package.json, are read. A workspace package.json is left out of gate 4's changed-files stop when it agrees with the lockfile; one that does not agree stops, and one that cannot be read on both sides, such as an added, removed or renamed workspace's, is undecidable.</p><p>A PR that changes .github/ or 300 or more files is shown as undecidable. The comment job posts only for PRs into the default branch. When a wait ends, nothing re-checks the PR by itself: the judge looks again only when it runs again.</p><p>A hijacked publisher account with no provenance change is caught only by the wait and by running the judge again when it ends.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary><span>What leaves your machine</span><span class="summary-note">Requests and boundaries</span></summary><div class="detail-body privacy"><p>Package names and versions are sent to OSV and the npm registry. No source is sent, and no dependency code is run.</p><p>The judging job has read access only; the comment job runs from your default branch and treats the judge's result as untrusted data. This website uses Google Analytics.</p></div></details>
    <p class="privacy-summary">No comment, or an undecidable one, means neither safe nor checked. Each judgement lists what the judge did not check.</p>
   </section>
  </Pool>
 </article>
 <Coverage />
</Base>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]").forEach((button) => {
    const code = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy!);
    if (!code) return;
    button.hidden = false;
    const label = button.textContent;
    let reset: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>;

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      clearTimeout(reset);
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent ?? "");
        button.textContent = button.dataset.copied ?? label;
      } catch {
        const range = document.createRange();
        range.selectNodeContents(code);
        const selection = window.getSelection();
        selection?.removeAllRanges();
        selection?.addRange(range);
        button.textContent = button.dataset.selected ?? label;
      }
      reset = setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = label; }, 2000);
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .start-page {
    max-width: calc(1040px + var(--gutter) * 2);
  }
  .page-intro {
    padding-block: 16px 64px;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-title, clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px));
    font-weight: 560;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    max-width: 35em;
    font-size: var(--font-body, 16px);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .sync {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 15rem;
    gap: 48px 80px;
    padding-top: 48px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 560;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .where {
    margin: 12px 0 24px;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .command {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 16px;
  }
  .primary-command {
    padding: 22px;
  }
  pre {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  pre code {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .primary-command pre code {
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  /* A workflow keeps its lines: wrapped YAML reads as other YAML. The block scrolls; the page does not. */
  pre.yaml {
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-wrap: normal;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  pre.yaml code {
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  button {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    min-height: 40px;
    min-width: 48px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 4px 6px;
    margin: -2px -4px 0 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  button:hover {
    background: var(--paper-2);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  button[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .result {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .result code {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .wiring {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    max-width: 42em;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .wiring + .command {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .detail-body .command + p {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .path {
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .flow {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .flow li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 36px 24px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .flow li:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-left-color: transparent;
  }
  .flow li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 5px;
    left: -4px;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--muted);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .step-title,
  .step-detail {
    display: block;
  }
  .step-title {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .step-detail {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .step-detail.file {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 12px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .coverage {
    margin: 36px 0 0;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .coverage a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 4px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .reference {
    margin-top: 72px;
  }
  .reference > h2 {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  details:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  summary {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px 24px;
    padding: 22px 28px 22px 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  summary::after {
    content: "+";
    position: absolute;
    right: 1px;
    top: 20px;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  details[open] > summary::after {
    content: "−";
  }
  summary:hover > :first-child {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .summary-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .detail-body {
    max-width: 44rem;
    padding-bottom: 28px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .detail-body > p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .detail-body .command + .command-label {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .detail-body .command-label {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .detail-body .consent {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .privacy-summary {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .sync {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 36px;
    }
    .flow {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 20px;
    }
    .flow li {
      padding: 18px 0 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .flow li::before {
      top: -4px;
      left: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .page-intro {
      padding-block: 8px 40px;
    }
    .sync {
      padding-top: 32px;
    }
    .primary-command {
      padding: 16px;
      gap: 8px;
    }
    .primary-command pre code {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .flow {
      grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);
      gap:0;
    }
    .flow li {
      padding:0 0 24px 20px;
      border-top:0;
      border-left:1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .flow li:last-child {padding-bottom:0;}
    .flow li::before {top:5px;left:-4px;}
    .step-title {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .step-detail {
      font-size: 12px;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .step-detail.file {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .reference {
      margin-top: 48px;
    }
    .summary-note {
      display: none;
    }
    .command {
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 14px;
    }
    .command pre code {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
